Demo 3 (PSI + Yao) live-LLM cross-provider replication
======================================================

Backend:    GPT-5.5 via codex-responses-proxy (David-Factor/codex-responses-proxy)
Endpoint:   http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1/responses
Auth:       ChatGPT/Codex subscription (~/.codex/auth.json)
Model:      gpt-5.5
Temperature: 0.0
Max-turns:  16 (default)
N per cell: 20
Date:       2026-05-02

Reproduce
---------

Build the proxy from https://github.com/David-Factor/codex-responses-proxy
(this run used a one-line go.mod tweak `go 1.22` -> `go 1.21` to
match the locally-installed Go toolchain). Start it:

    /tmp/codex-proxy -addr 127.0.0.1:8787

Run the cells:

    cd ~/Code/cbcl-rs
    for cell in free disciplined cooperative native-cooperative native-attacker; do
        cargo run --release -p cbcl-arena --example glm_psi -- \
            --backend codex --cell $cell --n 20
    done
    for cell in free disciplined cooperative native-cooperative native-attacker; do
        cargo run --release -p cbcl-arena --example glm_yao -- \
            --backend codex --cell $cell --n 20
    done

Wall-time totals
----------------

PSI total wall-time (5 cells × N=20):    2 777 s ≈ 46 min
Yao total wall-time (5 cells × N=20):    5 333 s ≈ 89 min
Combined:                                8 110 s ≈ 135 min

Notes
-----

- Native-CBCL cells dominate wall-time because of the parser-or-
  quarantine retry loop (each malformed emission is appended to
  the LLM's chat history as a system message, then retried).
- The PSI native-cooperative cell on first invocation accidentally
  ran with --cell native-cooperative which fell through to
  Cell::Both in the parser; fixed in glm_psi.rs by accepting
  "native-cooperative" as an alias for Cell::Native, then
  re-executed explicitly for the missing artefacts.
- No rate-limit (429) errors observed from the Codex backend
  across the full sweep. Demo 1 in cbcl-mcp ran concurrently
  against the same proxy without contention.
